WEBVTT

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.694
Dad wants us to pick
up where he left off --

00:00:04.694 --> 00:00:06.799
Saving people, hunting things.

00:00:06.799 --> 00:00:07.972
The family business.

00:00:09.666 --> 00:00:11.561
Anybody here?

00:00:12.152 --> 00:00:13.545
Dont move.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:16.773
Sam? Dean?

00:00:16.773 --> 00:00:17.916
Mom, you know these guys?

00:00:17.916 --> 00:00:20.121
I think these are
John Winchesters boys.

00:00:20.121 --> 00:00:22.146
Hey, Im Ellen. That's my daughter, Jo.

00:00:22.146 --> 00:00:23.519
You're not gonna hit me again, are you?

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:25.303
You called our dad, said you could help.

00:00:25.303 --> 00:00:26.055
Help with what?

00:00:26.055 --> 00:00:27.438
The demon, of course.

00:00:27.438 --> 00:00:28.882
How do you know about all this?

00:00:28.882 --> 00:00:30.506
Hey, I just run a saloon.

00:00:30.506 --> 00:00:32.871
Hunters have been known to
pass through now and again --

00:00:32.871 --> 00:00:36.219
Including your dada long time
ago. John was like family once.

00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:38.074
You think dad and
Ellen never had a thing?

00:00:38.074 --> 00:00:39.206
No way.

00:00:39.206 --> 00:00:41.141
Then why didn't he tell us about her?

00:00:42.825 --> 00:00:44.258
How did your mom get into this stuff?

00:00:44.258 --> 00:00:47.496
My dad. He was a hunter. He passed away.

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:48.358
I could help

00:00:48.358 --> 00:00:51.215
I'm sure you could, but I
think your mother might kill me.

00:00:51.215 --> 00:00:53.149
You're afraid of my mother?

00:00:53.741 --> 00:00:54.793
I think so.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:17.086
I checked the fuses. They're fine.

00:01:17.086 --> 00:01:18.840
It's the wiring!

00:01:19.231 --> 00:01:22.709
Look, you promised this place
would be ready when I moved in.

00:01:23.662 --> 00:01:26.057
No! You come up now!

00:01:26.418 --> 00:01:28.263
Please.

00:01:28.774 --> 00:01:30.538
Thank you.

00:01:39.579 --> 00:01:41.554
Gross.

00:02:18.432 --> 00:02:20.376
What the hell?

00:02:45.335 --> 00:02:47.370
Los Angeles, California.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:48.954
What's in L.A.?

00:02:48.954 --> 00:02:51.400
A young girl's been
kidnapped by an evil cult.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.593
Yeah?

00:02:53.034 --> 00:02:54.978
The girl got a name? Katie Holmes.

00:02:57.534 --> 00:03:01.153
That's funny.

00:03:05.543 --> 00:03:07.939
Of course, on the other hand, catfight.

00:03:07.939 --> 00:03:09.884
I am your mother! I don't
have to be reasonable!

00:03:09.884 --> 00:03:11.598
You can't keep me here!

00:03:11.598 --> 00:03:12.820
Don't you bet on that, sweetie!

00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:14.855
Are you gonna chain
me up in the basement?

00:03:14.855 --> 00:03:17.141
You've had worse ideas
than that recently.

00:03:17.141 --> 00:03:19.206
You don't want to stay?
Don't -Go back to school!

00:03:19.206 --> 00:03:22.032
I didn't belong there! I was a
freak with a knife collection!

00:03:22.032 --> 00:03:25.280
Getting yourself killed on some dusty
back road -That's where you belong?

00:03:30.182 --> 00:03:32.658
Guys, bad time. Yes, ma'am.

00:03:32.658 --> 00:03:34.903
We rarely drink before 10:00 anyway.

00:03:34.903 --> 00:03:36.226
Wait.

00:03:37.058 --> 00:03:38.582
I want to know what
they think about this.

00:03:38.582 --> 00:03:40.606
I don't care what they think!

00:03:40.606 --> 00:03:42.070
Are you guys open?

00:03:42.070 --> 00:03:43.593
Yes! No!

00:03:47.433 --> 00:03:50.219
We'll just check out
the Arby's down the road.

00:04:10.728 --> 00:04:12.382
Harvelle's.

00:04:12.382 --> 00:04:14.316
Yeah, preacher.

00:04:14.316 --> 00:04:17.364
Three weeks ago, a young girl
disappears from a Philadelphia apartment.

00:04:19.679 --> 00:04:20.902
Take it. It won't bite.

00:04:20.902 --> 00:04:23.338
No, but your mom might.

00:04:26.285 --> 00:04:30.204
And this girl wasn't the first. Over the
past 80 years,6 women have vanished --

00:04:30.204 --> 00:04:32.750
All from the same
building, all young blondes.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:35.346
It only happens every decade or two,
so cops never eyeball the pattern.

00:04:36.128 --> 00:04:38.694
So we're either dealing with
one very old serial killer --

00:04:38.694 --> 00:04:41.661
Who put this together? Ash?

00:04:41.661 --> 00:04:43.345
I did it myself.

00:04:46.402 --> 00:04:49.249
I got to admit, we hit
the road for a lot less.

00:04:49.249 --> 00:04:51.344
Good. If you like the
case so much, you take it.

00:04:51.725 --> 00:04:54.712
Joanna Beth, this
family has lost enough.

00:04:55.644 --> 00:04:57.689
I won't lose you, too.

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.809
I just wont.

00:05:05.087 --> 00:05:06.510
Mother told me

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:08.715
Yes, she told me

00:05:08.715 --> 00:05:11.983
I'd meet girls like you

00:05:11.983 --> 00:05:13.807
She also told me,

00:05:13.807 --> 00:05:15.802
"Stay away

00:05:15.802 --> 00:05:19.330
You'll never know what you'll catch"

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.205
Mommy's all right,

00:05:21.205 --> 00:05:22.678
Daddys all right,

00:05:22.678 --> 00:05:26.167
They just seem a little weird.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:29.755
Surrender, surrender.

00:05:31.028 --> 00:05:33.554
I feel kind of bad, snaking jobs case.

00:05:34.827 --> 00:05:37.574
Well, maybe she put
together a good file,

00:05:37.965 --> 00:05:40.791
But could you see her out here
working one of these things?

00:05:40.791 --> 00:05:42.666
I don't think so.

00:05:44.550 --> 00:05:45.914
You getting anything?

00:05:47.287 --> 00:05:48.921
No, not yet.

00:05:54.103 --> 00:05:55.677
What's that?

00:05:56.017 --> 00:05:57.531
What?

00:06:02.713 --> 00:06:04.678
Holy crap.

00:06:12.046 --> 00:06:14.161
That's ectoplasm.

00:06:14.391 --> 00:06:17.108
Well, Sam, I think I know
what we're dealing with here.

00:06:18.491 --> 00:06:20.886
It's the stay-Puft marshmallow man.

00:06:21.668 --> 00:06:25.507
Dean, Ive only seen
this stuff like twice.

00:06:25.507 --> 00:06:29.156
I mean, to make this stuff, you have
to be one majorly pissed-Off spirit.

00:06:30.179 --> 00:06:32.895
Let's find this badass before
he snags any more girls.

00:06:37.005 --> 00:06:39.350
Yeah, it's a great building.
I fixed it up real nice.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:40.744
All the apartments come furnished, too.

00:06:40.744 --> 00:06:44.523
Yeah, I love the
furnishings. It's so spacious,

00:06:44.523 --> 00:06:48.873
And the location is
so convenient for me.

00:06:48.873 --> 00:06:50.527
What the hell are you doing here?

00:06:50.527 --> 00:06:52.391
There you are, honey.

00:06:54.005 --> 00:06:56.411
This is my boyfriend,
Dean, and his buddy Sam.

00:06:56.411 --> 00:06:59.187
Good to meet you. Quite
a gal you got here.

00:06:59.187 --> 00:07:01.102
Yeah, she's a pistol!

00:07:01.272 --> 00:07:03.808
So, did you already
check out the apartment?

00:07:05.773 --> 00:07:07.457
The one for rent.

00:07:07.457 --> 00:07:10.755
Yeah. Yes. Loved it. Great flow.

00:07:10.755 --> 00:07:12.429
How'd you get in? It was open.

00:07:13.541 --> 00:07:16.188
Now, Ed, when did the
last tenant move out?

00:07:16.709 --> 00:07:19.395
Uh, about a month ago. Cut and run, too.

00:07:19.395 --> 00:07:20.408
Stiffed me for the rent.

00:07:20.408 --> 00:07:23.184
Well, her loss, our gain,

00:07:23.184 --> 00:07:25.530
'Cause if Dean loves it,
it's good enough for me.

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.484
Oh, sweetie.

00:07:28.146 --> 00:07:29.840
We'll take it.

00:07:32.486 --> 00:07:33.789
Okay.

00:07:37.167 --> 00:07:38.591
I'll flip you for the sofa.

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:39.954
Does your mother even know youre here?

00:07:39.954 --> 00:07:41.167
I told her I was going to Vegas.

00:07:41.167 --> 00:07:42.259
You think shes gonna buy that?

00:07:42.259 --> 00:07:43.142
I'm not an idiot.

00:07:43.142 --> 00:07:46.078
I got Ash to lay a credit-Card
trail all the way to the casinos.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:50.489
You shouldn't lie to your mom.
You shouldn't be here, either.

00:07:52.534 --> 00:07:55.551
Well, I am, so untwist your
boxers and deal with it.

00:07:55.551 --> 00:07:57.496
Where'd you get all
that money from, anyways?

00:07:57.496 --> 00:07:58.498
Working at the roadhouse.

00:07:58.498 --> 00:07:59.741
Hunters don't tip that well.

00:07:59.741 --> 00:08:01.746
They aren't that good at poker, either.

00:08:08.301 --> 00:08:10.045
Yeah? Is she with you?

00:08:11.128 --> 00:08:12.241
Oh, hi, Ellen.

00:08:12.241 --> 00:08:14.887
She left a note shes in Vegas.
I don't believe it for a second.

00:08:17.884 --> 00:08:19.488
Dean? I haven't seen her.

00:08:19.488 --> 00:08:21.753
You sure about that? Yeah, Im sure.

00:08:21.753 --> 00:08:24.891
Well, please, if she shows up, you'll
drag her butt back here, won't you?

00:08:24.891 --> 00:08:27.006
Absolutely. Okay. Thanks, hon.

00:08:31.707 --> 00:08:34.002
This place was built in 1924.

00:08:34.002 --> 00:08:37.370
It was originally a warehouse, converted
into apartments a few months ago.

00:08:38.282 --> 00:08:40.708
Yeah? What was here before 1924?

00:08:40.708 --> 00:08:42.091
Nothing. An empty field.

00:08:42.091 --> 00:08:43.976
So the most
likely scenario --

00:08:43.976 --> 00:08:47.254
Someone died bloody in the building,
and now he's back and raising hell.

00:08:48.727 --> 00:08:50.271
I already checked.

00:08:50.271 --> 00:08:52.977
In the past 82 years,
zero violent deaths,

00:08:52.977 --> 00:08:55.313
Unless you count a janitor
who slipped on a wet floor.

00:08:56.014 --> 00:08:58.149
Would you sit down, please?

00:09:01.257 --> 00:09:04.043
So, have you checked the police
reports, county death records?

00:09:04.043 --> 00:09:07.552
Obituaries, mortuary reports,
and seven other sources.

00:09:07.552 --> 00:09:08.624
I know what I'm doing.

00:09:08.624 --> 00:09:10.809
I think the jury's
still out on that one.

00:09:13.065 --> 00:09:15.350
Would you put the knife down?

00:09:15.731 --> 00:09:18.999
Okay. So, uh, its something else, then.

00:09:18.999 --> 00:09:21.645
Maybe some kind of cursed object
that brought a spirit with it.

00:09:21.645 --> 00:09:24.482
We got to scan the whole
building. Right. So, you and me --

00:09:24.482 --> 00:09:28.171
Well take the top two floors.

00:09:28.171 --> 00:09:30.396
We'd move faster if we split up.

00:09:30.396 --> 00:09:32.300
Oh, this isn't negotiable.

00:09:34.065 --> 00:09:36.310
So, are you gonna buy me dinner?

00:09:36.881 --> 00:09:38.565
What are you talking about?

00:09:38.936 --> 00:09:42.374
It's just if you're gonna ride me this
close, it's only decent you buy me dinner.

00:09:42.755 --> 00:09:44.329
Oh, that's hilarious.

00:09:44.329 --> 00:09:45.873
Its bad enough I lied to your mom,

00:09:45.873 --> 00:09:47.837
But if you think I'm letting
you out of my sight --

00:09:47.837 --> 00:09:50.323
I don't know if you noticed, but
you're kind of the spirit's type.

00:09:50.704 --> 00:09:52.047
Exactly.

00:09:52.949 --> 00:09:54.272
You want to be bait?

00:09:54.272 --> 00:09:56.117
The quickest way to draw
it out, and you know it.

00:09:56.718 --> 00:09:58.272
What? I'm so regretting this.

00:09:58.964 --> 00:10:01.399
I've had it up to herewith your crap.

00:10:02.181 --> 00:10:03.093
Excuse me?

00:10:03.093 --> 00:10:04.797
Your chauvinist crap.

00:10:04.797 --> 00:10:06.471
You think women cant do the job.

00:10:06.471 --> 00:10:10.030
Sweetheart, this ain't gender
studies. Women can do the job fine.

00:10:10.030 --> 00:10:12.416
Amateurs cant. You got no experience.

00:10:12.416 --> 00:10:17.046
What you do have is a bunch of half-Baked romantic
notions that some barfly has put in your head.

00:10:17.046 --> 00:10:18.690
And now you sound like my mother.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.906
Oh, and that's a bad thing?
Because let me tell you --

00:10:20.906 --> 00:10:22.850
What?

00:10:25.166 --> 00:10:26.790
Forget it.

00:10:26.790 --> 00:10:28.243
No, you started this.

00:10:28.243 --> 00:10:31.972
Jo, you got options. No one in
their right mind chooses this life.

00:10:31.972 --> 00:10:35.350
My dad started me in this when I was so
young. I wish I could do something else.

00:10:35.350 --> 00:10:36.583
You love the job.

00:10:36.583 --> 00:10:38.026
Yeah, but Im a little twisted.

00:10:38.026 --> 00:10:40.673
You don't think Im
a little twisted, too?

00:10:42.326 --> 00:10:44.622
Jo, you got a mother
that worries about you,

00:10:44.622 --> 00:10:47.960
Who wants something more for
you. Those are good things.

00:10:48.621 --> 00:10:51.348
You don't throw things like that away.

00:10:51.719 --> 00:10:54.074
They might be hard to find later.

00:11:31.523 --> 00:11:32.896
What?

00:11:35.693 --> 00:11:37.367
I'm not sure.

00:11:40.053 --> 00:11:41.537
Do you smell that?

00:11:43.091 --> 00:11:44.995
What is it, a gas leak?

00:11:44.995 --> 00:11:47.361
No. Its something else.

00:11:49.005 --> 00:11:52.844
I know it. I just can't
put my finger on it.

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:02.196
Mazel Tov. You just
found your first spirit.

00:12:03.419 --> 00:12:05.444
It's inside the vent.

00:12:12.089 --> 00:12:13.673
Here.

00:12:33.570 --> 00:12:35.214
There's something in there. Here.

00:12:57.938 --> 00:13:00.254
Someone's keeping souvenirs.

00:13:52.507 --> 00:13:54.773
This building --
I swear to god.

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:20.915
I'm so out of here.

00:15:03.406 --> 00:15:05.090
Morning, princess.

00:15:05.881 --> 00:15:08.157
Where's Sam? Went to get coffee.

00:15:13.159 --> 00:15:14.863
My back.

00:15:17.359 --> 00:15:20.256
How'd you sleep on that big, soft bed?

00:15:20.256 --> 00:15:21.909
I didnt.

00:15:21.909 --> 00:15:24.455
I've just been going over everything.

00:15:37.406 --> 00:15:39.020
Here.

00:15:39.020 --> 00:15:40.353
What's this for?

00:15:40.353 --> 00:15:43.771
It'll work a hell of a lot better than that
little pig stick you've been twirling around.

00:15:57.063 --> 00:15:59.699
William Anthony Harvelle.

00:16:02.125 --> 00:16:04.531
I'm sorry. My mistake.

00:16:15.296 --> 00:16:17.441
What do
you --

00:16:17.441 --> 00:16:19.436
What do you remember about your dad?

00:16:20.178 --> 00:16:23.145
What's the first thing
that pops into your head?

00:16:27.685 --> 00:16:29.971
Come on. Tell me.

00:16:37.819 --> 00:16:40.406
I was 6 or 7...

00:16:41.488 --> 00:16:43.663
And, uh...

00:16:44.205 --> 00:16:46.640
He took me shooting for the first time.

00:16:46.640 --> 00:16:49.698
Bottles on a fence
--That kind of thing.

00:16:51.011 --> 00:16:53.156
I bull's-Eyed every one of them.

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:58.408
And he would smile, like...

00:17:01.405 --> 00:17:03.129
I dont know.

00:17:05.345 --> 00:17:07.360
He must have been proud.

00:17:10.006 --> 00:17:12.301
What about your dad?

00:17:14.336 --> 00:17:17.183
I was still in pigtails
when my dad died, but...

00:17:18.105 --> 00:17:21.072
I remember him coming home from a hunt.

00:17:21.553 --> 00:17:23.949
He'd burst through
that door like --

00:17:24.149 --> 00:17:26.675
Like Steve McQueen or something.

00:17:27.547 --> 00:17:29.863
And he'd sweep me up in his arms,

00:17:30.234 --> 00:17:32.810
And I'd breathe in that
old leather jacket of his.

00:17:34.303 --> 00:17:37.471
And my mom --Who
was sour and pissed

00:17:37.471 --> 00:17:40.528
From the minute he left
She started smiling again.

00:17:41.571 --> 00:17:43.435
And we were...

00:17:44.698 --> 00:17:46.583
We were a family.

00:17:52.998 --> 00:17:55.604
You want to know why
I want to do the job?

00:17:56.446 --> 00:17:58.641
For him.

00:17:59.223 --> 00:18:01.738
It's my way of being close to him.

00:18:02.891 --> 00:18:05.026
Now, tell me, what's wrong with that?

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:08.404
Nothing.

00:18:14.819 --> 00:18:17.155
Where's the coffee?
There are cops outside.

00:18:18.137 --> 00:18:20.262
Another girl disappeared.

00:18:28.342 --> 00:18:30.898
Theresa Ellis
--Apartment 2-F.

00:18:30.898 --> 00:18:33.133
Her boyfriend reported
her missing around dawn.

00:18:33.133 --> 00:18:34.677
And her apartment?

00:18:34.677 --> 00:18:37.614
Cracks all over the
plaster --Walls, ceiling.

00:18:37.614 --> 00:18:39.127
There's ectoplasm, too.

00:18:39.127 --> 00:18:42.335
Between that and that tuft of hair, I'd
say the suckers coming from the walls.

00:18:42.335 --> 00:18:45.602
But who is it? The building's
history's totally clean.

00:18:48.008 --> 00:18:50.233
Maybe we're looking in the wrong place.

00:18:50.233 --> 00:18:52.820
What do you mean? Check this out.

00:18:56.488 --> 00:18:57.641
An empty field?

00:18:57.641 --> 00:19:01.440
It's where this building was built.
Take a look at the one next door.

00:19:02.803 --> 00:19:05.229
The windows.

00:19:07.174 --> 00:19:08.206
Bars.

00:19:08.206 --> 00:19:10.121
We're next door to a prison?

00:19:10.121 --> 00:19:11.374
Thanks, Ash.

00:19:11.374 --> 00:19:13.408
Oh, and if you breathe a
word of this to my mom --

00:19:13.408 --> 00:19:17.468
Thats right. I will. With pliers.

00:19:18.130 --> 00:19:20.465
Okay. Moyamensing
prison --

00:19:20.465 --> 00:19:24.254
Built in 1835, torn down
in 1963. And get this --

00:19:24.254 --> 00:19:28.113
They used to execute people by hanging
them in the empty field next door.

00:19:29.366 --> 00:19:32.634
Well, then, we need a list of
all the people executed there.

00:19:32.634 --> 00:19:34.609
Ash is already on it.

00:19:41.004 --> 00:19:43.700
157 names?

00:19:44.141 --> 00:19:46.186
We got to narrow that down. Yeah.

00:19:46.186 --> 00:19:48.873
Or else we're gonna be digging
up a hell of a lot of stiffs.

00:19:56.030 --> 00:19:58.004
Herman Webster Mudgett?

00:19:59.638 --> 00:20:01.392
Yeah?

00:20:02.365 --> 00:20:05.382
Wasn't that H.H. Holmes' real name?

00:20:06.895 --> 00:20:09.311
You got to be kidding me.

00:20:15.706 --> 00:20:19.094
Holmes was executed at
Moyamensing may 7,1896.

00:20:19.184 --> 00:20:21.350
H.H. Holmes himself.

00:20:21.761 --> 00:20:23.505
Come on. I mean, what are the odds?

00:20:23.505 --> 00:20:25.339
Who is this guy?

00:20:25.339 --> 00:20:28.677
The term "multi-Murderer" --
They coined it to describe Holmes.

00:20:28.677 --> 00:20:31.985
He was Americas first serial killer before
anybody knew what a serial killer was.

00:20:31.985 --> 00:20:35.513
He confessed to 27 murders, but
some put the death toll at over 100.

00:20:35.513 --> 00:20:39.122
And his victim flavor of
choice -Pretty, petite blondes.

00:20:39.523 --> 00:20:42.530
He, uh, used chloroform to kill them,

00:20:43.462 --> 00:20:45.838
Which is what I smelled
in the hallway last night.

00:20:47.973 --> 00:20:49.707
At his place, cops found human remains,

00:20:49.707 --> 00:20:53.335
Bone fragments, and long
locks of bloody blond hair.

00:20:53.335 --> 00:20:55.460
Boy, he sure knew how to pick them.

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:58.137
We just find the bones, salt
them, and burn them, right?

00:20:58.137 --> 00:20:59.470
It's not that easy.

00:20:59.470 --> 00:21:01.755
His body is buried in town,

00:21:01.755 --> 00:21:04.462
But it's encased in a
couple tons of concrete.

00:21:04.462 --> 00:21:06.176
What? Why?

00:21:06.176 --> 00:21:09.464
The story goes that he didn't
want anybody mutilating his corpse

00:21:09.464 --> 00:21:12.190
'Cause, you know, it's
what he used to do.

00:21:12.190 --> 00:21:14.105
You know something?

00:21:16.230 --> 00:21:18.094
We might have an even
bigger problem than that.

00:21:18.094 --> 00:21:20.079
How does this get bigger?

00:21:20.780 --> 00:21:23.046
Holmes built an apartment
building in Chicago.

00:21:23.046 --> 00:21:26.354
They called it the murder castle.
The whole place was a death factory.

00:21:26.354 --> 00:21:29.521
They had trapdoors, acid
vats, quicklime pits.

00:21:29.521 --> 00:21:32.137
He built these secret chambers...

00:21:32.137 --> 00:21:34.052
Inside the walls.

00:21:34.052 --> 00:21:36.267
He'd lock his victims in,
keep them alive for days.

00:21:36.267 --> 00:21:38.071
Some, he'd suffocate.

00:21:38.071 --> 00:21:40.207
Others, he'd let starve to death.

00:21:40.207 --> 00:21:44.256
So Theresa could still be alive.
She could be inside these walls.

00:21:44.256 --> 00:21:46.722
We need sledgehammers, crowbars.
We got to smash these walls

00:21:46.722 --> 00:21:48.987
Anywhere thick enough to hide a girl.

00:22:03.712 --> 00:22:07.110
Okay. Call us after you
check the southeast wall.

00:22:08.223 --> 00:22:11.050
Sam's almost done with the first floor.

00:22:11.521 --> 00:22:13.756
He hasn't found jack squat, either.

00:22:20.552 --> 00:22:21.795
What is it?

00:22:21.795 --> 00:22:24.351
It's too narrow. We
can't go any further.

00:22:24.351 --> 00:22:26.055
Let me see. -
What are you --

00:22:29.574 --> 00:22:31.478
I should have cleaned the pipes. What?

00:22:31.478 --> 00:22:33.934
I wish the pipes were clean.

00:22:34.465 --> 00:22:35.909
Shut up!

00:22:35.909 --> 00:22:37.432
I can fit in there.

00:22:37.823 --> 00:22:39.186
You're not going in thereby yourself.

00:22:39.186 --> 00:22:40.800
You got a better idea?

00:22:40.800 --> 00:22:42.234
The
--

00:23:05.529 --> 00:23:07.754
Where are you? By the north wall.

00:23:27.812 --> 00:23:30.749
I'm heading down some kind of air duct.

00:23:30.749 --> 00:23:32.583
No, no, no, no. Stay up here.

00:23:32.583 --> 00:23:34.718
We got to find this girl, don't we?

00:23:35.360 --> 00:23:36.793
I'm okay.

00:23:36.793 --> 00:23:38.738
All right. Im heading to you.

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:14.623
Oh, god.

00:24:15.254 --> 00:24:16.828
What is it?

00:24:17.730 --> 00:24:20.216
Jo? Jo?!

00:24:28.466 --> 00:24:29.869
Jo!

00:24:51.871 --> 00:24:53.645
Jo?!

00:24:56.021 --> 00:24:57.775
Jo!

00:25:07.037 --> 00:25:09.162
He's got Jo. What? Howd that happen?

00:25:09.162 --> 00:25:11.237
I wasn't with her. I
left her alone. Damn it!

00:25:11.237 --> 00:25:14.044
Look, we'll find her. Where? Inside
the walls. We were inside the walls.

00:25:14.044 --> 00:25:17.392
None of the other girls are
there. She won't be, either.

00:25:18.404 --> 00:25:21.221
Look, take a beat and think about
this. Maybe we got Holmes' M.O. Wrong.

00:25:21.221 --> 00:25:23.245
Well, we better friggin' think fast.

00:25:26.794 --> 00:25:27.686
Yeah?

00:25:27.686 --> 00:25:29.661
You lied to me. Shes there.

00:25:29.661 --> 00:25:31.976
Ellen. Ash told me everything.

00:25:31.976 --> 00:25:34.001
The man's a genius, but
he folds like a cheap suit.

00:25:34.001 --> 00:25:35.484
You put my damn daughter on the phone.

00:25:35.484 --> 00:25:38.913
She's gonna have to call you back. She's,
uh, taking care of feminine business.

00:25:38.913 --> 00:25:41.138
Yeah, right. Where is she?

00:25:41.609 --> 00:25:43.604
Where is she?!

00:25:44.045 --> 00:25:45.208
Look, we'll get her back.

00:25:45.208 --> 00:25:47.653
Get her back? Back from what?

00:25:47.653 --> 00:25:49.327
The spirit we're
hunting --It took her.

00:25:49.327 --> 00:25:50.049
Oh, my god.

00:25:50.049 --> 00:25:51.573
She'll be okay. I promise. You promise?

00:25:51.573 --> 00:25:55.452
That is not the first time Ive
heard that from a Winchester.

00:25:55.702 --> 00:25:56.575
What?

00:25:56.575 --> 00:25:58.499
If anything
happens to her --

00:25:58.499 --> 00:26:00.033
It wont. I won't let it.

00:26:00.033 --> 00:26:01.847
Ellen, Im sorry. I really am.

00:26:01.847 --> 00:26:04.543
I'm taking the first flight out.
I'll be there in a few hours.

00:26:07.009 --> 00:26:09.305
Damn it!

00:26:09.305 --> 00:26:12.372
Don't beat yourself up, Dean.
There's nothing you could have done.

00:26:12.372 --> 00:26:13.886
Tell me you got something.

00:26:13.886 --> 00:26:15.159
Uh, maybe.

00:26:16.602 --> 00:26:17.885
Look.

00:26:17.885 --> 00:26:19.659
If you look at the layout
of the Holmes murder castle,

00:26:19.659 --> 00:26:21.935
Theres other torture chambers
inside the walls, right?

00:26:22.356 --> 00:26:24.350
But there's one we
havent considered yet --

00:26:24.350 --> 00:26:25.714
The one in his basement.

00:26:25.714 --> 00:26:26.776
This building doesn't have a basement.

00:26:26.776 --> 00:26:29.442
You're right. It doesnt.
But I just noticed this.

00:26:29.533 --> 00:26:31.056
Beneath the foundation,

00:26:31.056 --> 00:26:33.272
It looks like part of an old sewer
system. It hasn't been used for --

00:26:33.272 --> 00:26:34.725
Lets go.

00:27:45.493 --> 00:27:46.826
Hello?

00:27:56.860 --> 00:27:58.844
Is -Is anybody there?

00:27:59.476 --> 00:28:01.862
Your name's Theresa?

00:28:03.275 --> 00:28:04.959
Yes.

00:28:04.959 --> 00:28:07.816
This won't make you feel better, but...

00:28:08.387 --> 00:28:10.602
I'm here to rescue you.

00:28:11.234 --> 00:28:14.401
Oh, god. He's out there.
He's gonna kill us!

00:28:14.401 --> 00:28:16.476
No, he won't!

00:28:16.476 --> 00:28:18.752
We're getting out.

00:28:18.752 --> 00:28:21.468
My friends are looking for us.

00:28:22.360 --> 00:28:24.225
Oh, god, it's him!

00:28:24.225 --> 00:28:26.540
Shh! Just be quiet!

00:29:28.297 --> 00:29:29.920
Here.

00:29:57.045 --> 00:29:58.719
Got it? Yeah.

00:31:00.926 --> 00:31:02.570
You're so pretty.

00:31:06.700 --> 00:31:08.614
So beautiful.

00:31:08.614 --> 00:31:10.639
Go to hell!

00:31:43.658 --> 00:31:45.281
How do you like that?!

00:31:45.281 --> 00:31:48.279
Pure iron, you
creepy-Ass son of a bitch!

00:32:51.909 --> 00:32:53.744
Is he gone?

00:32:54.816 --> 00:32:56.821
I don't
know. I --

00:33:14.724 --> 00:33:16.367
Hey!

00:33:17.420 --> 00:33:18.773
No!

00:33:20.337 --> 00:33:21.580
Jo!

00:33:22.001 --> 00:33:23.755
I'm here!

00:33:48.233 --> 00:33:50.158
Hey. I'm gonna get you
out of here, all right?

00:33:50.689 --> 00:33:52.343
Sam!

00:33:54.658 --> 00:33:56.362
Hang on.

00:33:59.239 --> 00:34:01.855
You all right? I've been better.

00:34:02.407 --> 00:34:05.013
Let's get the hell out of
here before he comes back.

00:34:05.013 --> 00:34:08.060
Actually, I don't think
you're leaving here just yet.

00:34:08.060 --> 00:34:08.742
What?

00:34:08.742 --> 00:34:11.328
Remember when I said you
being bait was a bad plan?

00:34:11.328 --> 00:34:13.483
Now it's kind of the only one we got.

00:35:28.611 --> 00:35:29.934
Now!

00:35:49.581 --> 00:35:53.520
Scream all you want! There's no
way you're stepping over that salt!

00:36:04.095 --> 00:36:05.759
So...

00:36:05.759 --> 00:36:08.476
Is this job as glamorous
as you thought it would be?

00:36:09.498 --> 00:36:11.894
Well, except for all the
peeYour-Pants terror, yeah.

00:36:12.555 --> 00:36:15.322
But that Theresa girl's gonna
live a life 'cause of us.

00:36:15.693 --> 00:36:16.986
It's worth it, isn't it?

00:36:16.986 --> 00:36:18.419
Yeah.

00:36:18.419 --> 00:36:19.873
Yeah, it is.

00:36:19.873 --> 00:36:21.817
Hey, what if somebody
finds that sewer done there

00:36:21.817 --> 00:36:23.722
Or a storm washes the salt away?

00:36:23.722 --> 00:36:27.050
Both very fine points, which
is why we're waiting here.

00:36:27.050 --> 00:36:28.563
For what?

00:36:34.998 --> 00:36:36.642
For that.

00:36:57.933 --> 00:36:59.877
You ripped off a cement truck?

00:36:59.877 --> 00:37:01.391
I'll give it back.

00:37:16.868 --> 00:37:20.015
Well, that ought to keep him
down there till hell freezes over.

00:37:53.695 --> 00:37:57.203
Well, you -You really weren't
kidding about flying out, were you?

00:38:10.565 --> 00:38:12.640
How about we listen to some music?

00:38:13.382 --> 00:38:16.439
You're as cold as ice.

00:38:27.074 --> 00:38:29.290
This is gonna be a long drive.

00:38:36.998 --> 00:38:38.762
Ellen...

00:38:38.762 --> 00:38:42.631
It was my fault. Okay? I
lied to you, and I'm sorry.

00:38:42.631 --> 00:38:44.897
But Jo did good out there. I
think her dad would be proud.

00:38:44.897 --> 00:38:47.583
Don't you dare
say that --Not you.

00:38:47.583 --> 00:38:50.219
I need a moment with
my daughter -Alone.

00:38:59.281 --> 00:39:00.834
You're angry. I understand.

00:39:00.834 --> 00:39:02.729
Angry doesn't beg into touch it!

00:39:02.729 --> 00:39:05.385
Let's just think about
this. Everything's okay.

00:39:05.385 --> 00:39:06.879
I'm alive.

00:39:06.879 --> 00:39:08.422
Not after Im through with you!

00:39:08.422 --> 00:39:09.856
Is this about me hunting
or something else?

00:39:09.856 --> 00:39:11.480
You let those boys use you as bait.

00:39:11.480 --> 00:39:13.254
They were backing me up the whole time.

00:39:13.254 --> 00:39:15.168
That is why you do not have
the sense to do this job.

00:39:15.168 --> 00:39:16.912
You're trusting your life to
them. What are you talking about?

00:39:16.912 --> 00:39:19.278
Like father, like son.
That is what Im talking...

00:39:24.591 --> 00:39:26.345
John?

00:39:28.881 --> 00:39:31.086
I thought you and John were friends.

00:39:31.086 --> 00:39:33.211
Yeah, we were. I'm
sorry. I didn't mean --

00:39:33.211 --> 00:39:34.624
Mom...

00:39:37.321 --> 00:39:39.907
What aren't you telling me?

00:39:56.156 --> 00:39:58.020
That bad, huh? Not right now.

00:39:59.624 --> 00:40:01.298
What happened? Hey, talk to me.

00:40:01.298 --> 00:40:02.972
Get off me!

00:40:03.553 --> 00:40:05.357
Sorry. Ill see you around.

00:40:05.357 --> 00:40:07.573
Dean...

00:40:11.412 --> 00:40:14.519
It turns out my dad had a
partner on his last hunt.

00:40:14.519 --> 00:40:16.804
Funny, he usually worked
alone. This guy did, too.

00:40:16.804 --> 00:40:20.814
But I guess my father
figured he could trust him.

00:40:21.576 --> 00:40:25.275
A mistake. The guy screwed
up, got my dad killed.

00:40:25.275 --> 00:40:27.640
What does this have --
It was your father, Dean.

00:40:28.663 --> 00:40:30.206
What?

00:40:30.206 --> 00:40:33.825
Why do you think John never came
back, never told you about us?

00:40:33.825 --> 00:40:36.732
'Cause he couldn't look my mom
in the eye after that -That's why.

00:40:37.173 --> 00:40:38.877
Jo --
Just --

00:40:38.877 --> 00:40:41.112
Just get out of here.

00:40:41.954 --> 00:40:43.798
Please, just leave.

00:00:02.469 --> 00:00:03.973
